One thing to know: object keys are always strings, so `id` will be a string even if your IDs look like numbers. If you need numbers, use `id: Number(id)`.

Order matters too. Keys that look like non-negative integers (`"3"`, `"17"`) come out first, in ascending numeric order, and the rest follow in the order the keys were added. If your IDs are numeric and you want them sorted, sort the array afterwards.

If you ever need to go back the other way:

```js
const asObject = Object.fromEntries(
  data.properties.map(({ id, fieldValue }) => [id, fieldValue])
);
```

