A few things are worth saying about it.

The type parameter `<T>` is there so you can reuse the same structure for different parents. Set `T` to `String` if the parent is just a category name. Set `T` to a `Codable` type if each expense has its own data, such as a budget limit or a colour.

Firestore does not allow documents inside other documents. Every document lives at its own path. So the real paths look like this:

```
expenses/{expenseId}
expenses/{expenseId}/months/{monthId}
expenses/{expenseId}/months/{monthId}/days/{dayId}
expenses/{expenseId}/months/{monthId}/days/{dayId}/orders/{orderId}
